id: ops-release-changelog-stability
title: Keep release changelog bytes stable when the pending version becomes a tag
description: "Release commit 32ecf1e passes generation before v2026.10.26 exists, but the fetched tag makes the full generator emit an empty Unreleased section and changelog:check fails. The earlier empty-release fix remains valid. Investigate the independent immutable v2026.10.20 repair blocker without rewriting release evidence."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T02:55:44.757Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T04:00:36.947Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Real tracker regression commits and tags a pending release and proves changelog:check still passes with exactly one section per version; The regression fails when only the changed generation behavior is reverted; Regenerate with fetched tags and pass npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds; Run release completeness verification and record any immutable historical blocker without publishing or changing tags; Open a PR with tracker evidence and green CI, leaving it unmerged"
resolution: "Normalize the generator-supplied empty Unreleased window above release history through the shared adapter used by generation, checks and notes. Preserve empty version sections and nonempty unreleased work. Leave final review and closure to the orchestrator."
expected_result: "Committing and tagging a pending release preserves changelog:check and exactly one dated section per release, retaining meaningful unreleased work."
actual_result: "Real tracker regression and source-only revert proof verified. Both local release gates pass 1468 tests with 2 opt-in skips and 100% in all coverage dimensions across 39 measured sources. Current changelog has 60 sections for 60 tags. The independent historical completeness audit still reports one missing GitHub Release, tracked in ops-release-1020-recovery."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T02:55:53.555Z",codex-agent,"Comparison confirms v2026.10.20:CHANGELOG.md has no 2026.10.20 section. Current main and v2026.10.26 each have exactly one such section: it was not lost or duplicated by the new release. Repair reads notes from the immutable 2026.10.20 commit, so its missing GitHub Release remains ops-release-1020-recovery. The new stale-main cause is separate: include-empty emits an empty Unreleased window only after the pending version becomes a real tag. Plan: normalize that empty non-release window while retaining every version section and all nonempty unreleased work, then exercise the complete commit/tag/check transition with a real tracker."
  "2026-10-27T02:58:46.624Z",codex-agent,"The release log confirms changelog:check passed at 14:42:02Z and the repair refused historical notes at 14:50:20Z. Normalization now drops only the generator-supplied empty Unreleased heading above version history. Regression covers real committed tracker snapshots, pending-to-tag byte equality, empty releases, a same-day suffix, and retained nonempty unreleased work. Full gates will run under bounded CPU affinity so Node uses at most two test workers. The live read-only completeness command still reports one missing GitHub Release, v2026.10.20."
  "2026-10-27T03:00:11.286Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only describeEmptyReleases to the pre-fix implementation makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='release commits stay' test/changelog-sections.test.ts fail (0 passed, 1 failed) at the first post-tag changelog:check, with Changelog is out of date. Restoring the fix passes all three release transitions (1 passed, 0 failed). The regression imports the TypeScript source directly, so no dist rebuild is needed for this proof."
  "2026-10-27T03:02:41.172Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test run passed 6/6 with no failures or skips; test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains the result. Regenerating the original 32ecf1e tree with all fetched tags adds exactly four lines: an empty Unreleased heading and No tracked changes. Current changelog:full and changelog:check pass; 60 release tags map to 60 sections with zero cardinality mismatches. Current main had already regenerated the file in #211, so regeneration adds no file diff. The guarded exact workflow command, npm run verify:release-completeness -- --repair, still exits 1 at immutable 2026.10.20 notes before any mutation; GitHub writes were blocked by a local read-only guard."
  "2026-10-27T03:12:35.922Z",codex-agent,"Opening the review candidate after focused tests and revert proof, while the full isolated npm gate continues. GitHub CI can run independently while local npm/Bun verification completes. The PR will remain unmerged and its validation section will state the pending gates until their results are known. Historical v2026.10.20 generation scripts and release workflow both lacked include-empty, confirming the original missing-window cause."
  "2026-10-27T03:18:59.411Z",codex-agent,"PR #216 is open: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/216, code commit 75894ff115d4fd137714979e467d2ec06a6875f8. The isolated npm run release:check passed: 1470 total, 1468 passed, 0 failed, 2 opt-in real-data skips; 39 measured source files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, docstrings, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack dry run, changelog, date, publish-attestation and lifecycle checks passed. Strict tracker health also passed. Bun gate is next, with two workers via CPU affinity. Automated review is unavailable: CodeRabbit skipped by repository policy, Sourcery quota exhausted, Greptile trial ended, and cubic was neutral. None is counted as approval."
  "2026-10-27T03:21:59.922Z",codex-agent,"Code commit 75894ff115d4fd137714979e467d2ec06a6875f8 passed all four PR CI matrix jobs: test (22), test (26), windows-consumers (22), windows-consumers (26). CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40442905062. CodeQL also passed. Local Bun release gate remains in progress; final tracker evidence will be committed and its exact PR head checked before handoff. No merge is requested or performed."
  "2026-10-27T03:39:42.141Z",codex-agent,"The first local Bun gate failed at an unchanged test: regular-input.test.ts, all artifact readers refuse special inputs. Its child process exceeded the existing five-second timeout while cold-loading the SDK; the FIFO case stopped before assurance.ts and index.ts refusal branches, leaving 99.95% aggregate branch coverage. Result: 1467 passed, 1 failed, 2 opt-in skips. All changelog cases passed and PR CI passed on Node 22/26. Investigating the focused input test, then rerunning Bun with one worker and unchanged test/coverage thresholds. This failure is not being counted as a passing gate."
  "2026-10-27T03:43:03.897Z",codex-agent,"The focused regular-input file also timed out (5 passed, 1 failed). A diagnostic measured about 3.5 seconds between preload and completed imports before any input assertions, so the five-second wall deadline includes substantial startup cost; the exact timed-out phase is not yet proven. Follow-up ops-input-startup-timeout tracks the separate timing issue. A focused retry without restricted CPU affinity and a complete diagnostic trace are being used before another full gate attempt. No test deadline, assertion or coverage threshold is changed."
  "2026-10-27T03:44:31.885Z",codex-agent,"The unchanged input-boundary control now passes 6/6 both with unrestricted one-worker execution and with a different two-CPU affinity (one test worker). Instrumented real FIFO refusal completed all eight consumers within roughly 20 milliseconds after imports, with about 1.5 seconds of import startup in that successful run. The full isolated Bun gate is being repeated with one worker; no source, timeout, test set or coverage threshold was changed. The earlier failure remains recorded under ops-input-startup-timeout."
  "2026-10-27T04:00:32.697Z",codex-agent,"Final local gate results: npm run release:check and the one-worker bun run release:check both pass, each with 1470 total tests, 1468 passed, 0 failed and 2 opt-in real-data skips. Both measure 39 source files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines, with unchanged thresholds. All remaining release checks pass, including production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack dry run, changelog, date, publish-attestation and lifecycle policy. The first two-worker Bun timeout remains in ops-input-startup-timeout; no test deadline or assertion changed. Refreshed read-only npm run verify:release-completeness still reports exactly one missing GitHub Release, v2026.10.20. The guarded workflow repair command previously reproduced the immutable-note refusal with one failure. That audit cannot pass through generator changes alone, and release creation is forbidden by the queue rules. Keep ops-release-1020-recovery open. PR #216 code CI and CodeQL passed; the final tracker evidence commit will receive exact-head CI before handoff."
